    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">"Sustainable packaging" usually sounds like something that costs more — compostable mailers, premium recycled papers, certification fees. Reused carton boxes are the exception: the greenest common packaging choice in Malaysia is also the cheapest one. Here's why the used carton is a genuine win-win for your business and the environment.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Reuse Beats Recycling</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Recycling a carton is good; reusing it is better. Recycling still means trucking the box to a mill, pulping it with water and energy, and manufacturing new board. Reuse skips the entire loop — the box simply carries goods again. Every carton that does a second or third trip displaces a brand-new box that never has to be made, and corrugated board is sturdy enough to make several journeys before it finally enters the recycling stream.</p>

        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">The Numbers for Your Business</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Used cartons cost 40-60% less than new — RM 1.90-3 versus RM 3-6 for a medium box. A business shipping 500 parcels a month saves roughly RM 1,000-1,500 monthly, or up to RM 18,000 a year, simply by changing where it buys boxes. There is no other sustainability initiative that pays you from day one with zero process change. For the full comparison, see our <a href="/blog/new-vs-used-carton-boxes" class="text-primary underline">new vs used guide</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Customers Reward It — If You Tell Them</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Consumer surveys across Southeast Asia consistently show that a majority of shoppers — strongest among under-35s — prefer brands with sustainable packaging. The trick is communication: an unexplained scuffed box looks like corner-cutting, but the same box with a small sticker reading "this carton is on its second journey" reads as a brand with values. Some of our customers print thank-you cards explaining the reuse policy; several report it's their most-mentioned feature in reviews.</p>

        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Quality Concerns, Answered</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">The common worry is strength and cleanliness. Graded used cartons — the only kind worth buying — are single-trip factory boxes inspected for crush damage, moisture, tears, and odours. For parcels under 20kg with normal handling, they protect goods as well as new boxes. Reserve new cartons for heavy, fragile, or presentation-critical shipments and run everything else on reused stock.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="bg-surface-variant/50 border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-8 my-12">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">The Win-Win at a Glance</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="font-label text-primary font-bold text-sm mb-2">COST</p>
